          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Sagan's Contribution to Space Exploration</strong><br>\nCarl Sagan's influence on space exploration was profound. He advised NASA on the Mariner, Viking, Voyager, and Galileo space missions, helping to shape their scientific goals. He consistently advocated for robotic space missions and was a voice for science in policy and education, emphasizing the need for a scientific understanding in the broader public.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Sagan's Views on Science and Society</strong><br>\nSagan was a vocal advocate for the use of scientific knowledge to address global issues. He warned about the dangers of nuclear war and climate change, stressing humanity's responsibility to use technology wisely. His promotion of skepticism and scientific inquiry influenced public thought on a variety of scientific and existential questions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Carl Sagan</strong><br>\nCarl Sagan passed away on December 20, 1996, leaving behind a legacy as a teacher, scientist, and communicator. His ability to capture the public's interest in science has had a lasting impact, fostering a sense of wonder about the universe. His work continues to inspire future generations to look up at the stars and ponder their place in the cosmos.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
